## Architecture Decision — My Recommendation

**Keep FastAPI. Do NOT switch to Django.**

Your Study7 makes the Django case well for a greenfield hospital system. But you're not starting from zero — you have 40+ routers, 30+ services, a working EOS agent framework, auth, workflow engine, and audit logging already built and tested. Throwing that away and rebuilding in Django would cost 3–4 months of lost ground. FastAPI handles relational, integrity-sensitive data fine through Supabase + Pydantic schemas. The right call is:

> **FastAPI = Synbot Health overlay + gradual HMS (Phase 1–4)**
> Django Admin = optional internal management panel if needed (Phase 3+, additive not replacement)

This matches your own strategy: overlay first, phase the incumbent out. FastAPI IS the overlay layer.

